WEBVTT

00:02.841 --> 00:04.900
So you understand the situation?

00:05.077 --> 00:06.510
I think so.

00:06.678 --> 00:09.545
Now that we're not married anymore
you wanna sell my condo.

00:09.715 --> 00:12.684
No, no. It's our condo. I got it for us.

00:12.851 --> 00:18.414
Not the smartest thing I ever did,
but my real-estate adviser was my penis.

00:18.957 --> 00:22.415
Is that what they mean
when they say the market's gone soft?

00:23.628 --> 00:25.289
I don't think so.

00:25.897 --> 00:28.559
My point is, I can't afford
to carry the mortgage.

00:28.734 --> 00:31.396
But if we sell it,
then we can split the profit.

00:31.570 --> 00:33.162
Or I could buy you out.

00:33.638 --> 00:36.766
- Do you have money?
- I will after we sell.

00:37.476 --> 00:39.103
Kandi, I am at the end of my rope.

00:39.277 --> 00:43.236
If I can't get out from under these bills,
I may well have to declare bankruptcy.

00:43.415 --> 00:44.848
Wow.

00:45.016 --> 00:48.417
- That sounds really serious.
- It is. Deadly serious.

00:49.254 --> 00:52.087
Well, in that case...

00:53.525 --> 00:55.186
...wanna have sex?

00:55.360 --> 00:58.022
- What?
- I'm horny, you're stressed...

00:58.196 --> 00:59.857
...seems like we'd both benefit.

01:00.565 --> 01:02.829
Well, I am really stressed.

01:03.101 --> 01:04.898
No, that's not gonna solve anything.

01:05.070 --> 01:07.834
Okay, well, I'm gonna go take a shower.

01:08.006 --> 01:11.100
- Let me know if you change your mind.
- I changed my mind.

01:18.984 --> 01:21.384
I either drank too much...

01:21.553 --> 01:24.078
...or got hit by a train.

01:27.659 --> 01:31.095
- Oh, God, train.
WoMAN: Charlie?

01:34.065 --> 01:35.157
Oh, look.

01:35.534 --> 01:38.560
It's my sweet angel
come to take me to heaven.

01:38.970 --> 01:40.767
Don't touch me.

01:41.907 --> 01:43.465
I hope you're proud of yourself.

01:43.642 --> 01:44.973
Well...

01:45.143 --> 01:48.408
...I didn't wake up in my own vomit,
so, yeah, kind of.

01:50.182 --> 01:52.412
You are such a child.

01:52.584 --> 01:55.610
Many people find that
to be an endearing quality.

01:56.087 --> 01:58.180
I'm not one of them.

01:58.557 --> 02:00.616
It would appear not.

02:02.060 --> 02:05.757
- We had fun last night, though, right?
- Oh, terrific.

02:05.931 --> 02:08.627
What woman doesn't enjoy
pleasing a man who falls asleep...

02:08.800 --> 02:11.667
...while he's in the middle
of reciprocating?

02:12.704 --> 02:16.367
Well, that explains why I dreamt
I was kissing Abe Lincoln.

02:19.411 --> 02:21.743
Uh-oh.

02:29.454 --> 02:30.512
Okay.

02:30.689 --> 02:31.849
Just some underwear.

02:32.023 --> 02:33.786
No need to panic.

02:34.426 --> 02:37.020
And a little bit of makeup. No biggie.

02:37.929 --> 02:41.421
Running shoes, reading glasses,
flannel nightgown...

02:41.600 --> 02:44.160
&lt;i>...and the latest issue
of Modern Bride magazine.&lt;/i>

02:45.003 --> 02:46.868
Red alert.

02:47.906 --> 02:50.067
Lydia?
What?

02:52.110 --> 02:56.137
I couldn't help but notice that you put
some of your stuff in one of my drawers.

02:56.314 --> 03:00.250
Yeah. Hey, you wanna come
in here and make up for last night?

03:00.685 --> 03:03.848
Well, yeah, but I think we should talk
about this drawer thing.

03:04.322 --> 03:05.346
Okay.

03:06.691 --> 03:08.158
Talk.

03:11.596 --> 03:13.894
Four score and seven years ago...

03:14.065 --> 03:17.660
...our fathers brought forth upon
this continent a new nation.

03:48.566 --> 03:50.033
Morning.

03:50.568 --> 03:53.628
That was a great shower.

03:54.639 --> 03:59.133
Yeah. You know, it's good when you feel
dirtier coming out than you did going in.

04:00.345 --> 04:02.779
- So, what are you doing?
- Just practicing.

04:02.948 --> 04:04.472
- For what?
- Nothing in particular.

04:04.649 --> 04:08.779
- Just keeping sharp for my work.
- Oh, yeah, your little jingle thing.

04:10.755 --> 04:13.121
Hard to believe that takes practice.

04:21.599 --> 04:25.660
Berta, I'd like some scrambled egg whites,
dry wheat toast and Earl Grey tea.

04:25.837 --> 04:30.536
Oh, yeah? Well, I'd like some new shoes,
a jetpack and a waistline.

04:36.414 --> 04:39.679
You really thought
she was gonna make you breakfast.

04:46.157 --> 04:48.557
- Yo, bro.
- Hey.

04:48.727 --> 04:50.854
- How'd it go with Kandi?
- Great.

04:51.029 --> 04:52.690
Just great.

04:53.098 --> 04:55.862
Turns out we can be friends
with benefits.

04:56.301 --> 04:58.701
Nice. And did she agree
to sell the condo?

04:58.870 --> 04:59.962
What?

05:00.839 --> 05:03.603
Isn't that why you went over there
in the first place?

05:03.775 --> 05:05.572
Oh, yeah.

05:06.811 --> 05:09.473
Son of a bitch.

05:09.647 --> 05:11.012
Charlie...

05:11.583 --> 05:13.346
...you need to talk to your maid.
- Shh-shh!

05:13.518 --> 05:16.385
- Keep your voice down.
- Yeah, we don't use the M-word here.

05:16.554 --> 05:17.646
Why not?

05:17.822 --> 05:19.653
- Because it's disrespectful.
- Demeaning.

05:19.824 --> 05:21.724
And wildly inaccurate.

05:25.997 --> 05:28.795
The point is, Berta's the one
who keeps this house running...

05:28.967 --> 05:30.867
...and more important, she's like family.

05:31.036 --> 05:33.402
She's rude, offensive and vulgar.

05:33.805 --> 05:36.501
Okay, exactly like family.

05:36.941 --> 05:38.169
Fine.

05:38.343 --> 05:43.110
See if she'll do that thing with the ice cubes
and the silk handkerchief you like so much.

05:43.281 --> 05:45.010
Come on, sweetie, don't be like that.

05:45.784 --> 05:47.513
Ice cubes and a silk handkerchief?

05:47.685 --> 05:50.210
You can also use a Popsicle
and a necktie.

05:51.089 --> 05:53.853
But I do owe you a silk handkerchief.

05:55.326 --> 05:58.022
And your water pick's kind of iffy.

06:00.365 --> 06:04.426
And whatever you do,
don't lick your hairbrush.

06:10.241 --> 06:12.675
I'm sorry to come over here
and bother you again.

06:12.844 --> 06:15.472
We never finished talking
about selling the condo.

06:15.647 --> 06:17.274
But I don't wanna sell the condo.

06:17.449 --> 06:19.212
I can see boats from here.

06:20.018 --> 06:23.385
I understand,
but I can't afford the payments.

06:23.555 --> 06:26.149
I like boats.

06:27.425 --> 06:30.053
All right, well if you won't cooperate...

06:30.228 --> 06:33.493
...I'll just have to call my lawyer.
What are you doing?

06:33.932 --> 06:36.765
Chester lost his bone. I'm looking for it.

06:36.935 --> 06:38.800
Now? Can't it wait?

06:38.970 --> 06:42.838
No. When Chester wakes up
from his nap, he's gonna want his bone.

06:43.007 --> 06:44.565
You can keep talking.

06:45.877 --> 06:51.907
Okay, well, as I said, if you won't be
reasonable, I'll just have to...

06:54.552 --> 06:56.816
Have to what, Alan?

06:57.489 --> 07:00.458
Son of a bitch.

07:09.300 --> 07:11.131
What the...?

07:12.604 --> 07:13.935
We need to talk.

07:18.176 --> 07:20.906
- Okay.
- I don't mind your girlfriends...

07:21.079 --> 07:24.071
...throwing the occasional thong
or panties into the hamper.

07:24.249 --> 07:27.116
I just boil them
and sell them at the swap meet.

07:27.852 --> 07:31.652
But this broad is taking advantage
of my easy-going nature.

07:33.158 --> 07:37.561
Now, to be fair,
Lydia does have her positive attributes.

07:37.729 --> 07:41.859
Yeah, well, I ain't hitting any of them
attributes, so I don't give a rat's ass.

07:42.734 --> 07:43.962
All right, all right.

07:44.135 --> 07:46.228
You know what she said to me, Charlie?

07:46.404 --> 07:48.702
She said I need to learn
my place around here.

07:49.140 --> 07:50.630
Oh, she didn't.

07:50.808 --> 07:53.368
Ah, but she did.

07:54.546 --> 07:56.241
Is that true, Charlie?

07:56.414 --> 07:59.542
Do I need to learn my place around here?

08:00.585 --> 08:01.916
No, we all know your place.

08:02.086 --> 08:04.384
- Where is that place?
- Wherever you want it to be.

08:04.556 --> 08:07.582
There is only room for one alpha dog
in this house.

08:07.759 --> 08:09.659
- I know.
- Who is that alpha dog, Charlie?

08:09.827 --> 08:10.851
- You are.
- Say it.

08:11.029 --> 08:12.587
- You're the alpha dog.
- Aw.

08:12.864 --> 08:14.195
You sweet talker you.

08:16.768 --> 08:19.635
We'll just pretend that's morning wood.

08:33.918 --> 08:36.113
Hey, how's it going?

08:36.287 --> 08:38.653
Well, look who's finally up.

08:38.823 --> 08:40.518
I need some lotion on my back.

08:40.992 --> 08:43.017
Oh, sure.

08:43.194 --> 08:45.424
Listen, I have to talk to you about Berta.

08:46.231 --> 08:48.961
For God's sake, Charlie, grow a pair.

08:51.236 --> 08:52.533
Is this your house or hers?

08:53.004 --> 08:56.235
Well, my name's on the deed,
but she was here first.

08:56.741 --> 08:59.266
Thing is, over the years,
Berta and I have developed...

08:59.444 --> 09:01.435
...a really nice working relationship and...

09:01.613 --> 09:03.410
Do my thighs.

09:05.683 --> 09:06.707
Right.

09:06.884 --> 09:10.376
And the key to a happy home,
I find, is to not rock the boat...

09:10.555 --> 09:12.147
...not tamper with that balance.

09:12.323 --> 09:15.258
- You need to make the effort to treat her...
- Where is she now?

09:15.426 --> 09:17.587
Huh? She went shopping.

09:17.762 --> 09:19.389
Anybody else around?

09:20.265 --> 09:22.028
No. Anyway, the thing with Berta...

09:22.200 --> 09:24.828
Why don't you put sunscreen
on your cute little bottom?

09:25.703 --> 09:28.934
- What for?
- I wouldn't want you to get a nasty burn.

09:29.641 --> 09:30.835
Why would I get a nasty...?

09:33.111 --> 09:35.011
Oh, you mean sex.

09:36.047 --> 09:38.413
Good thing you're pretty
because you're very slow.

09:43.721 --> 09:46.485
"Who's the alpha dog, Charlie?"

09:47.425 --> 09:49.825
"Grow a pair, Charlie. "

09:53.298 --> 09:55.493
Hey, Alan, come here.

09:56.267 --> 09:57.734
What's going on?

09:57.902 --> 09:59.233
I'm doing Lydia's laundry.

09:59.671 --> 10:02.139
Can I throw in my handkerchief?

10:03.308 --> 10:05.833
It wouldn't help.
You probably have to burn it.

10:06.778 --> 10:09.576
Okay. And why are you doing
Lydia's laundry?

10:09.747 --> 10:11.146
Because Berta won't.

10:11.316 --> 10:14.911
- Then why doesn't Lydia do it herself?
- Because I told her I'd get Berta to do it.

10:15.086 --> 10:16.348
Aha.

10:16.521 --> 10:18.318
Do you have any idea how to do laundry?

10:18.489 --> 10:20.980
You wash them, you dry them,
how tough could it be?

10:21.159 --> 10:23.093
So, what do you need me for?

10:23.828 --> 10:26.228
Which one's the washer?

10:29.334 --> 10:32.428
- That one.
- Thanks.

10:33.671 --> 10:35.605
Just kidding, it's that one.

10:37.742 --> 10:39.733
Sorry, it was the first one.

10:40.712 --> 10:42.976
Look, it says "wash" on the dial.

10:44.382 --> 10:48.045
Okay. Okay, I can do this.
I just turn it on and stick them in.

10:48.219 --> 10:51.916
It's a washing machine,
not a cocktail waitress.

10:52.924 --> 10:55.392
Let's start by separating her delicates.

10:56.561 --> 10:59.086
How is that not like a cocktail waitress?

11:01.099 --> 11:04.034
The reason you do these separately
is they're mostly synthetic.

11:04.202 --> 11:08.639
Add a beat-up Civic and an ex-husband
and we're back to cocktail waitress.

11:09.574 --> 11:11.974
Charming. Hand me the detergent.

11:12.143 --> 11:13.667
This stuff here?

11:13.845 --> 11:17.406
No, no, that's fabric softener.
You put that in after the first rinse cycle.

11:20.618 --> 11:23.485
You know what?
Maybe I'll just buy her some new clothes.

11:24.489 --> 11:26.252
Don't be such a baby.

11:26.424 --> 11:29.257
Detergent. See?

11:29.427 --> 11:31.691
There we go.

11:32.430 --> 11:36.662
Cold wash, cold rinse,
gentle cycle, done.

11:38.536 --> 11:39.730
What's that?

11:41.773 --> 11:44.241
That would be water entering
the washing machine.

11:45.943 --> 11:47.843
Amazing.

11:49.080 --> 11:51.446
Yeah, it's pretty cutting edge.

11:59.223 --> 12:00.247
Did I break it?

12:01.826 --> 12:03.418
Close the lid.

12:07.532 --> 12:09.523
Son of a gun.

12:22.313 --> 12:24.042
What will they think of next?

12:25.550 --> 12:28.178
Yeah, I hear scientists are working
on a machine...

12:28.352 --> 12:31.480
...that can cook two pieces of bread
at the same time.

12:38.095 --> 12:40.063
Yeah, yeah, yeah, very funny.
Now what?

12:40.231 --> 12:41.721
We wait.

12:41.899 --> 12:44.163
- How will we know when they're done?
- Don't worry.

12:44.335 --> 12:47.168
The machine will call you
on your cell phone.

12:47.738 --> 12:49.365
Really?

12:57.048 --> 12:59.983
I don't know what Berta's always
complaining about. This is fun.

13:00.151 --> 13:02.551
Well, you're dealing
with pretty girl underwear.

13:02.720 --> 13:06.520
Berta's gotta handle Jake's skivvies
after P.E. And pudding pops.

13:07.158 --> 13:08.819
Good point.

13:09.727 --> 13:12.355
- What are you doing?
- Pouring a glass of vodka.

13:12.530 --> 13:15.988
Is that part of doing the laundry?
Because I could really get into this.

13:16.367 --> 13:18.062
No, I'm just mad at myself.

13:18.536 --> 13:20.663
Well, in that case, pour me one.

13:20.838 --> 13:22.271
I'm mad at you too.

13:25.042 --> 13:27.670
- So, what's the problem?
- I went over to Kandi's again.

13:28.079 --> 13:29.273
And how did that go?

13:29.447 --> 13:31.312
Not only are we not selling the condo...

13:31.482 --> 13:33.609
...I may have promised to buy her
a new fridge.

13:34.318 --> 13:35.785
- Alan.
- She likes getting ice...

13:35.953 --> 13:37.580
...without having to open the door.

13:38.089 --> 13:39.886
You poor whipped sap.

13:40.057 --> 13:42.719
- Me? What about you?
- What about me?

13:42.894 --> 13:44.987
- Charlie, you're doing a womars laundry.
- No.

13:45.162 --> 13:47.027
That's just me trying to pitch in.

13:47.198 --> 13:49.928
Face it. Lydia's got you
wrapped around her little finger.

13:50.101 --> 13:51.864
She does not.

13:52.603 --> 13:54.628
She uses this one.

13:55.706 --> 13:59.437
And it's not so much wrapped
as skewered.

14:01.546 --> 14:03.377
Who's using my washing machine?

14:03.814 --> 14:07.750
Excuse me, but it's my washing machine
and I'm using it to wash Lydia's clothes.

14:07.919 --> 14:09.250
You're doing laundry?

14:09.420 --> 14:11.479
Hey, it's not rocket science.

14:11.656 --> 14:13.590
Cold wash, cold rinse, gentle cycle.

14:13.758 --> 14:16.056
But first, you separate the delicates.

14:16.227 --> 14:18.161
- Is that so?
- Yeah, that's so.

14:20.765 --> 14:22.733
That's probably them now.

14:25.336 --> 14:26.860
Hello?

14:27.038 --> 14:29.939
Oh, hey, Mom.
I thought you were my washing machine.

14:40.785 --> 14:43.310
Oh, come on, throw the ball,
throw the ball.

14:44.522 --> 14:46.649
Or fall down.

14:48.392 --> 14:51.259
- Charlie, I'm leaving.
- Bye.

14:53.531 --> 14:54.691
I'd like a kiss.

15:01.405 --> 15:03.532
She's still there, isn't she?

15:04.542 --> 15:05.873
Yep.

15:06.444 --> 15:08.105
Just kidding, sweetie.

15:08.279 --> 15:09.712
That's better.

15:09.880 --> 15:10.938
Goodbye, Jake.

15:11.449 --> 15:12.882
I'm not kissing you.

15:13.351 --> 15:17.048
Charlie, I almost forgot. I'm serving
hors d'oeuvres at an open house tomorrow.

15:17.221 --> 15:19.189
So I'll borrow Berta
for a couple of hours.

15:19.357 --> 15:21.325
Say what?

15:21.492 --> 15:22.789
I'm talking to Charlie.

15:22.960 --> 15:24.222
You don't mind, do you?

15:25.029 --> 15:28.487
- Mind? Well, I...
- You wanna borrow me?

15:28.666 --> 15:31.396
What am I, a carpet steamer?

15:31.702 --> 15:35.138
I'm not saying I won't pay you.
Plus, you can take home all the leftovers.

15:35.306 --> 15:39.538
Why don't you just toss them all in
a big bowl and I'll eat them out in the yard.

15:39.910 --> 15:42.970
That's a little uncalled for.
I thought I was doing you a favor.

15:43.147 --> 15:46.082
You wanna do me a favor?
Take the money you were gonna pay me...

15:46.250 --> 15:48.878
...convert it into rolls of nickels,
then bend over and...

15:49.053 --> 15:51.146
Berta, Berta, Berta.

15:54.659 --> 15:58.322
I don't have to stand here and listen
to this. You have to make a decision.

15:58.496 --> 16:01.363
It's her or me.

16:01.532 --> 16:03.432
The skank's right, Charlie.

16:04.835 --> 16:05.927
It's her or me.

16:09.473 --> 16:10.906
Great.

16:11.175 --> 16:13.541
That's just great.

16:14.078 --> 16:17.104
Did somebody say there was
a big bowl of food?

16:22.687 --> 16:24.621
You got an offer on the condo?

16:24.789 --> 16:27.189
Oh, Mom, you're a lifesaver.

16:27.358 --> 16:29.724
I don't care.
I fully expect to take a loss.

16:29.894 --> 16:32.522
At least I don't have to pay you
a commission.

16:32.963 --> 16:35.193
Oh, come on, you're my mother.

16:35.733 --> 16:38.224
Wait, wait. Hang on,
I've got another call coming in.

16:38.402 --> 16:42.668
Hello? Oh, Kandi. Kandi, hello.
Yeah, listen, about the condo.

16:42.840 --> 16:45.809
My mom just got
a very reasonable offer and...

16:46.610 --> 16:48.908
I give up, what are you wearing?

16:49.647 --> 16:52.775
Hang on. Mom, I gotta go.
Kandi, I'll be right there.

16:57.221 --> 16:58.711
Hey, is Berta here?

16:59.090 --> 17:01.456
- I haven't seen her.
- Great.

17:01.625 --> 17:04.594
&lt;i>I admit, I never thought you'd have
the cojones to fire Berta.&lt;/i>

17:04.762 --> 17:06.559
Are you kidding?

17:06.731 --> 17:10.132
&lt;i>I've got huge cojones. Why do you think
I wear these baggy shorts?&lt;/i>

17:14.105 --> 17:16.335
Wait, wait, wait. You fired Berta?

17:17.208 --> 17:18.835
Yes, Alan.

17:19.009 --> 17:21.239
She didn't know her place
and she had to go.

17:21.412 --> 17:23.004
But we can't live without Berta.

17:25.116 --> 17:26.674
I'll be right there, sweetie.

17:26.851 --> 17:28.375
Hurry.

17:29.854 --> 17:32.584
You know what? We need to work
on our communication skills.

17:32.757 --> 17:33.849
I always thought that.

17:34.024 --> 17:36.993
- I didn't think you'd be open...
- No, no, no, you jackass.

17:38.596 --> 17:41.929
God, you play along like a monkey
with a mandolin.

17:43.067 --> 17:46.264
- You mean you didn't fire Berta?
- That's it, give me the mandolin.

17:46.437 --> 17:48.428
You promised Berta
you'd get rid of Lydia.

17:49.273 --> 17:51.935
- Alan, do you know what this is?
- No.

17:52.109 --> 17:53.872
Then shut your stupid mouth.

17:54.845 --> 17:56.938
And don't tell Berta she was here.

17:57.114 --> 17:59.344
Fine. Just give me a heads up
when you're lying.

17:59.750 --> 18:02.150
I'm always lying.

18:02.653 --> 18:04.814
I'll give you a heads up when I'm not.

18:04.989 --> 18:07.685
Yeah, you're the smart one.
Know how I know?

18:08.259 --> 18:11.160
The washing machine called and told me.

18:17.735 --> 18:19.862
Ooh! High heels and Cool Whip.

18:29.980 --> 18:32.642
Oh, Charlie, how could you?

18:33.250 --> 18:36.083
Berta, this is not what it looks like.

18:36.253 --> 18:37.811
Charlie, you lied to me.

18:38.255 --> 18:40.849
Lydia, this is not what it looks like.

18:42.026 --> 18:44.494
- That's it, I'm out of here.
Me too.

18:44.662 --> 18:47.893
Berta? Lydia? Come on, wait.
This is not what it looks like.

18:50.201 --> 18:53.329
Say it a few more times, Charlie.
Maybe somebody'll believe you.

18:58.809 --> 19:01.869
Berta. Berta, Berta, Berta. Wait, wait, wait.
You can't quit.

19:02.046 --> 19:05.038
- Why not?
- Because we're family. We love each other.

19:05.216 --> 19:08.276
- We forgive each other our shortcomings.
- Oh, bite me.

19:08.853 --> 19:10.218
Don't go. Don't go.

19:10.387 --> 19:12.412
I promise I'll break it off with her.

19:12.590 --> 19:16.185
No, you won't. And you wanna know why?
Because you are addicted to this broad.

19:16.360 --> 19:19.295
